---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research & Tooling"
  description="Automated PRISMA metadata pipeline scaffold and exploratory CI diagnostic prototypes for game engine systems."
  image="/research/forest_plot_ci_timeouts.png"
>
  <!-- ============================================================
       HEADER & MASTHEAD
       ============================================================ -->
  <header class="research-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span>Software Engineering &amp; Research Tooling</span>
      <span class="eyebrow-badge">Automation Scaffold &middot; Synthetic Prototypes</span>
    </div>
    <div class="wayrule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <h1 class="display h1">PRISMA Automation Scaffold &amp; Game CI Diagnostic Toolchain</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Python Metadata Pipeline Architecture &amp; Exploratory CI Prototypes</p>

    <p class="lede">
      An automation architecture designed to orchestrate the mechanical stages of systematic literature reviews—from CrossRef and arXiv API querying to statistical synthesis and programmatic PDF compilation—paired with exploratory diagnostic prototypes for game engine CI build timeouts and crash log triage.
    </p>

    <!-- Prominent Artifact Disclaimer -->
    <div class="disclaimer-banner" role="note">
      <div class="disclaimer-badge">Disclaimer</div>
      <p class="disclaimer-text">
        These artifacts (manuscript PDFs, forest plots, and triage logs) are automated outputs generated by the pipeline scaffolding to demonstrate the tooling architecture, not real scientific publications. All underlying review records and crash traces are synthetically generated placeholder data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Primary Action Callouts -->
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <!-- Manuscript Download Link -->
      <a class="btn-cobalt" href="/research/Meta_Analysis_Manuscript.pdf" download="Meta_Analysis_Manuscript.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span> Download Sample Output Manuscript (PDF)
      </a>

      <!-- Showcase GitHub Repository Link -->
      <a class="btn-outline" href="https://github.com/akilfernando/quest-outreach-showcase" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span> View Showcase Repository on GitHub
      </a>

      <span class="meta-tagline">Author: Akil Fernando &middot; Dalhousie CS Alumni &middot; Teams Squared</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============================================================
       1. CANDIDATE QUALIFICATION TRIAD
       Highlighting: CS Degree | Game Industry Exp | AI Automation
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    01 / Engineering Pillars &amp; Background
    <span>CS Degree &middot; Ubisoft Game Dev &middot; Toolchain Automation</span>
  </h2>

  <div class="triad-grid">
    <!-- Pillar 1: Computer Science Degree & Academics -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">PILLAR I</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">BSc in Computer Science</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">
          Graduated from <strong>Dalhousie University (GPA 3.92, Sexton Scholar, Dean’s List)</strong> with certificates in Cybersecurity and Web/Mobile Systems. Strong foundation in software architecture, algorithm design, empirical research methodologies, and statistical analysis.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Academic credentials">
        <li>Dalhousie University</li>
        <li>GPA 3.92 / 4.30</li>
        <li>Sexton Scholar</li>
        <li>Research Methods</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <!-- Pillar 2: Game Industry Engineering Experience -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">PILLAR II</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">Game Industry Experience</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">
          Former <strong>Gameplay Programmer at Ubisoft Halifax</strong> working on production C# and Unity pipelines, Cinemachine camera systems, and AI behavior trees. First-hand domain insight into multi-gigabyte binary asset baking, physics frame-loop non-determinism, and cross-language (C++/C#) crash debugging.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Game development stack">
        <li>Ubisoft Halifax</li>
        <li>Unity &amp; C#</li>
        <li>Asset Pipelines</li>
        <li>Engine Debugging</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <!-- Pillar 3: End-to-End Diagnostic Automation -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">PILLAR III</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">Pipeline &amp; Toolchain Automation</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">
          Hands-on proficiency in autonomous developer toolchains: orchestrating Python, .NET 8, and modern AI tooling (<strong>Claude Code</strong>, <strong>Google Antigravity</strong>) to build diagnostic workflows, API ingestion pipelines, statistical calculation engines, and report compilers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Toolchain proficiency">
        <li>Python &amp; .NET 8</li>
        <li>API Ingestion</li>
        <li>Claude Code &amp; Antigravity</li>
        <li>Automation Pipelines</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       2. PRISMA METADATA PIPELINE SCAFFOLD
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    02 / PRISMA Systematic Review Automation Pipeline
    <span>API Ingestion &middot; Statistical Synthesis &middot; Automated PDF Compilation</span>
  </h2>

  <!-- Pipeline Stages Row -->
  <div class="metrics-bar">
    <div class="metric-cell">
      <div class="metric-num display">API &rarr; Ingest</div>
      <div class="metric-title">Automated Retrieval</div>
      <p class="metric-desc">Programmatic querying of CrossRef &amp; arXiv APIs with rate limiting and schema filtering.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="metric-cell">
      <div class="metric-num display">scipy / stats</div>
      <div class="metric-title">Statistical Engine</div>
      <p class="metric-desc">Automated calculation of random-effects meta-analysis models and effect sizes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="metric-cell">
      <div class="metric-num display">reportlab</div>
      <div class="metric-title">Document Compiler</div>
      <p class="metric-desc">Direct compilation of publication-ready structured PDF manuscripts from pipeline data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="metric-cell">
      <div class="metric-num display">Synthetic</div>
      <div class="metric-title">Validation Fixtures</div>
      <p class="metric-desc">Simulated study cohorts used to stress-test statistical routines and layout rendering.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Embedded Forest Plot & Architectural Discussion -->
  <div class="analysis-container">
    <!-- Forest Plot Figure Container -->
    <figure class="figure-frame">
      <img
        src="/research/forest_plot_ci_timeouts.png"
        alt="Sample Random-Effects Forest Plot generated automatically by the Python visualization pipeline to test layout rendering"
        loading="lazy"
        width="1200"
        height="750"
      />
      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        <strong>Figure 1 &middot; Automated Output Sample (matplotlib):</strong> Forest plot dynamically generated by the Python visualization pipeline to test rendering formatting, confidence intervals, and effect size plotting across simulated study cohorts. Not a real empirical publication.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Architectural Breakdown -->
    <div class="synthesis-text">
      <div class="synthesis-block">
        <h3>Automating Systematic Review Mechanical Steps</h3>
        <p>
          Systematic reviews following PRISMA 2020 guidelines require meticulous record-keeping across search queries, screening phases, data extraction, and statistical pooling. This pipeline automates the mechanical data flow—reducing human transcription errors and providing a repeatable, code-defined review lifecycle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="synthesis-block">
        <h3>Architecture &amp; Data Pipeline Layers</h3>
        <p>
          The architecture connects three decoupled stages: (1) an API client layer querying academic metadata endpoints with rate-limiting backoff; (2) a statistical calculation module utilizing <code>scipy</code> and <code>pandas</code> for effect size pooling and heterogeneity estimation; and (3) a document generator using <code>reportlab</code> to assemble formatted manuscripts complete with structured tables and references.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="synthesis-block">
        <h3>Synthetic Stress-Testing</h3>
        <p>
          To validate edge cases in the statistical engine and PDF layout engine before running on live empirical literature reviews, the pipeline uses synthetically generated test matrices. This verifies that layout bounding boxes, table pagination, and statistical convergence behave predictably under varying data distributions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       3. EXPLORATORY CI DIAGNOSTIC PROTOTYPES
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    03 / Exploratory CI Diagnostic Prototypes
    <span>Simulated Telemetry Predictor &middot; Memory-Normalized Crash Triage</span>
  </h2>

  <!-- Toolchain Submodule Cards -->
  <div class="toolchain-grid">
    <div class="tool-card">
      <p class="tool-tag">Prototype 01 &middot; Python ML Pipeline</p>
      <h3 class="tool-title display">CI Timeout Analyzer</h3>
      <p class="tool-desc">
        Exploratory prototype evaluating how build phase durations correlate with continuous integration timeouts in game engine pipelines using Random Forest regression on simulated telemetry.
      </p>
      <ul class="tool-features">
        <li>Build log phase segmentation (extracting asset cooking, compilation, and Link-Time Optimization phases).</li>
        <li>Feature extraction on asset delta volume and dependency graph modifications.</li>
        <li>Random Forest classification for early-warning timeout threshold prediction.</li>
        <li>Heuristic build optimization recommendations (e.g. distributed object caching and compiler flags).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <p class="tool-tag">Prototype 02 &middot; .NET 8 / C# Engine</p>
      <h3 class="tool-title display">Game Engine Crash Log Triage</h3>
      <p class="tool-desc">
        High-throughput stack trace normalization and clustering prototype that strips volatile runtime pointers and applies deterministic rule-based Git commit mapping across simulated crash archetypes.
      </p>
      <ul class="tool-features">
        <li>Memory-independent stack frame normalization (stripping dynamic pointers to canonical SHA-256 hashes).</li>
        <li>Automated deduplication clustering across noisy raw stack trace collections.</li>
        <li>Deterministic heuristic mapping from call stack frames to suspect Git commits and AST changes.</li>
        <li>Tested against simulated failure archetypes (NodePath breaks, thread disposal races, signal leaks).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Terminal Execution Proof Block -->
  <div class="terminal-wrapper" role="region" aria-label="Crash Triage Engine Execution Log">
    <div class="terminal-header">
      <div class="terminal-controls" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="control-dot dot-red"></span>
        <span class="control-dot dot-yellow"></span>
        <span class="control-dot dot-green"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-title">godot_triage_engine.exe &middot; Terminal Output</div>
      <div class="terminal-badge">SYNTHETIC FIXTURE DEMO &middot; ARCHITECTURAL PROOF</div>
    </div>

    <pre class="terminal-content"><code><span class="t-banner">===========================================================================
    EXPLORATORY GAME ENGINE CRASH LOG TRIAGE & FAULT LOCALIZATION ENGINE
           Synthetic Fixture Pipeline & Stack Normalization Demo
===========================================================================</span>

<span class="t-step">[Step 1/4]</span> Ingesting raw C# crash log fixtures (simulated game-engine failure modes)...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Ingested 50 synthetic crash logs with dynamic memory addresses and timestamps.

<span class="t-step">[Step 2/4]</span> Executing memory-independent stack frame normalization & SHA-256 deduplication...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Formed 6 unique crash clusters from 50 raw logs.
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Normalized dynamic pointers across all frames into canonical cluster hashes.

<span class="t-step">[Step 3/4]</span> Running heuristic fault localization & Git commit mapping on simulated fixtures...
   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_01] NodePath Resolution Failure (Scene Reparenting)</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.NullReferenceException</span>
     - Occurrences: 9 logs (18.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">a3f89b1c7d...</span> ("refactor(scene): move WeaponHolder node under CharacterRig hierarchy")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Combat/WeaponController.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Core.Combat.WeaponController._Ready()</span>
     - Root Cause    : Stale NodePath string literal in WeaponController._Ready(). Hierarchy was refactored, moving WeaponHolder under CharacterRig without updating the path constant.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_02] Null PhysicsDirectBodyState3D Reference in _PhysicsProcess</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.NullReferenceException</span>
     - Occurrences: 9 logs (18.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">c4d7e2a9b8...</span> ("feat(physics): implement asynchronous raycast sweep for character movement")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Physics/PlayerCharacter3D.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Core.Physics.PlayerCharacter3D._PhysicsProcess(Double delta)</span>
     - Root Cause    : Missing null check on KinematicCollision3D.GetCollider(). Asynchronous raycasts and concurrent body despawns leave the collider reference null upon slide resolution.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_03] Shader Uniform Buffer Layout Binding Mismatch</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">Engine.GraphicsException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">f9a8b7c6d5...</span> ("feat(rendering): add chromatic aberration and vignette compute shader")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Rendering/CustomPostProcessPipeline.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Rendering.CustomPostProcessPipeline.CreateComputePipeline()</span>
     - Root Cause    : UniformSet layout descriptor mismatch at binding index 2. Compute shader was updated to require a new uniform buffer, but UniformSetCreate was passed an outdated descriptor array.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_04] Multi-Threaded RenderingServer Race Condition on Scene Unload</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.ObjectDisposedException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">e1f2a3b4c5...</span> ("perf(world): offload voxel chunk mesh generation to background Task workers")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/World/ChunkRenderer.cs &rarr; GameEngine.World.ChunkRenderer.AsyncMeshUpdateWorker()</span>
     - Root Cause    : Cross-thread Object disposal race condition. ChunkRenderer dispatches async background Task workers that access engine pointers while the main thread frees chunks during scene unloading.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_05] Signal Emission to Disposed UI Callable Target</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">Engine.SignalException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">b2c3d4e5f6...</span> ("ui(hud): recreate player health bar widget on scene respawn")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Gameplay/HealthComponent.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Gameplay.HealthComponent.ApplyDamage(Single amount)</span>
     - Root Cause    : Signal emission to a stale Callable on a disposed UI instance. HealthComponent emits HealthChanged to a widget queued for deletion without unhooking signal handlers.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_06] NavigationAgent3D Empty Path Waypoint Index Overflow</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.IndexOutOfRangeException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">d8e9f01a2b...</span> ("ai(navigation): optimize waypoint path stepping for patrol agents")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/AI/EnemyNavigationController.cs &rarr; GameEngine.AI.EnemyNavigationController.GetNextSteeringVector()</span>
     - Root Cause    : IndexOutOfRangeException in EnemyNavigationController. Path query returned an empty Vector3 array during dynamic navigation mesh rebaking, causing an unchecked index [0] access.

<span class="t-step">[Step 4/4]</span> Exporting structured triage results to JSON artifact...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Structured triage results saved to: <span class="t-file">'triage_engine_results.json'</span>

<span class="t-banner">===========================================================================
               TRIAGE ENGINE EXECUTION COMPLETE
===========================================================================</span>
 Total Simulated Logs Processed  : <span class="t-accent">50</span>
 Unique Crash Clusters Isolated  : <span class="t-accent">6</span>
 Deduplication Normalization Rate: <span class="t-success">88.0%</span>
 Heuristic Commit Matches        : <span class="t-success">6/6 archetypes localized</span>
 Generated Output Artifact       : <span class="t-file">triage_engine_results.json</span>
<span class="t-banner">===========================================================================</span></code></pre>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       4. CITATION & ARTIFACT METADATA
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="citation-card">
    <h4>Software Repository &amp; Toolchain Reference</h4>
    <pre class="citation-box"><code>@software&#123;fernando2026prismapipeline,
  title=&#123;PRISMA Systematic Review Automation Scaffold and CI Diagnostic Prototypes&#125;,
  author=&#123;Fernando, Akil&#125;,
  year=&#123;2026&#125;,
  url=&#123;https://github.com/akilfernando/quest-outreach-showcase&#125;,
  note=&#123;Exploratory software pipeline and synthetic diagnostic prototypes&#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.4rem); margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .research-hero { margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* Disclaimer Banner */
  .disclaimer-banner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--cobalt);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--cobalt);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .disclaimer-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    background: var(--cobalt);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  .disclaimer-text {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .btn-cobalt {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: var(--cobalt);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 13px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--cobalt);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-cobalt:hover {
    background: var(--cobalt-deep);
  }
  .btn-outline {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 13px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-outline:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .meta-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .eyebrow-badge {
    background: var(--cobalt-tint);
    color: var(--cobalt);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sec-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .sec-label span {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* Triad Grid */
  .triad-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .triad-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .triad-card {
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    position: relative;
  }
  .triad-card::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
    background: var(--rule);
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .triad-card:hover::before {
    background: var(--cobalt);
  }
  .triad-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .triad-title {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
  .triad-body {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .triad-pills {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: auto;
  }
  .triad-pills li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    padding: 3px 9px;
  }

  /* Metrics Bar */
  .metrics-bar {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .metrics-bar { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .metrics-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .metric-cell {
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }
  .metric-num {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.8vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--cobalt);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .metric-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .metric-desc {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* Forest Plot Analysis */
  .analysis-container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1040px) {
    .analysis-container { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .figure-frame {
    background: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }
  .figure-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .figure-caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .figure-caption strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .synthesis-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
